<div class="text-center">
	<h1>
		Summary (1993 - Paris - Dakar)
	</h1>
	<p>
		<img src="1993_map.jpg" alt="" style="float:left; height: 131px;" />
		<img src="1993_01.jpg" alt="" style="float:right;" />
		Mitsubishi was never a manufacturer to rest on its laurels, and
		so the Pajeros were entered in the 15th running of the Dakar with the same seriousness
		as ever, even though the previous year the Pajero had achieved everything there was to achieve
		and had effortlessly prevailed over all others at the epic Paris - Moscow - Beijing rally.<img src="1993_02.jpg" alt="" style="float:left; height: 118px;" />
		Only 12 weeks after the rally through Russia and China,
		the team was ready for action again at the Dakar, which this time ended as usual&nbsp;
		in Senegal. One hundred and fifty-two competitors started on this occasion
		and set off into the desert to cover more than 9,000 km. The rally was
		remembered as one of the fastest ever. Like an unstoppable machine,
		Saby forced his way to the front and brought his Pajero home in first
		place.
	</p>
